    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e0b3ddde-a7b4-569c-ade5-2bbce0873822" activityNameId="0d7e0599-9812-5a98-acad-7870506e9cd8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, production BR, at service station</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, production BR, at service station
The inventory for "ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, production BR, at CH" is modelled with data of the regional distribution of petrol in Switzerland. The transports are modelled with the distance Brazil - Rotterdam for the transoceanic transport, the distance Rotterdam - Basel for the transport from the Netherlands to Switzerland,  and standard  distances for transports in Switzerland.;
CAS number: 000064-17-5; 
Formula: C2H6O ; 
Synonyms: Alkohol, alcohol dehydrated, algrain, Anhydrol, cologne spirit, cologne spirits (alcohol), Denatured alcohol, Ethyl alcohol, Ethanol, ethanol 200 proof, Ethanol absolute, ethyl hydrate, ethyl hydroxide, fermentation alcohol, grain alcohol, ; 
UUID: 4b9aea13-9f53-34c3-b0cf-15cba034815f
Supply of ethanol  from Brazilian production to service stations in Swtzerland including ethanol production and transports.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Switzerland with transports from Brazil to Switzerland. 
Technology: Production of ethanol from biomass.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: World ethanol production was around 276 Mio hl in 2003.
Sampling: Literature data. 
Extrapolations: Transports in Switzerland are modelled with standard distances. The distribution in Switzerland is modelled with regional distribution of petrol.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4b9aea13-9f53-34c3-b0cf-15cba034815f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
